-- the one row a contributor's local database needs before the dashboard is served and a donation form
-- can be added, applied by hand with `pnpm db:seed` (./seed.ts).
--
-- **not a migration, and it runs on no deployment.** migrations/ is applied by the two paths
-- CLAUDE.md → Bans names and this is neither of them; the values below are invented, so a
-- deployment that took them would be soliciting gifts under a registration that does not exist.
-- it is also not a file an organisation edits — CLAUDE.md → Product surface keeps the repository
-- free of those, and what makes this one exempt is that it is a fixture for a database that is a
-- cache: the local database file is deleted and rebuilt whenever the state goes stale, and this is
-- what fills it again.
--
-- **it finishes two of the five set-up jobs, both of them rows on `org_profile`**
-- (src/lib/server/config/readiness.ts): `organisation`, which is the registered name and the EIN
-- a donation form is refused without, and `notifications`, which is the address operational mail
-- goes to. the gate in src/routes/_app.tsx draws the set-up screen in place of every dashboard
-- screen until all five read done.
--
-- **the other three are nothing this file could write.** `payments` and `smtp` are deploy-time
-- values a contributor puts in `.env` (src/lib/server/config/env.ts) and never rows, and
-- `password` is one too. so a checkout that has run this still meets the gate on those three, and
-- that is the whole of what is left.
--
-- **no `site` row is seeded and none is needed.** a checkout serves its own donation page on the
-- app's own route at `/donate` (src/routes/donate.tsx), which takes gifts without being ticked
-- onto any site.
--
-- **three campaigns, one in each layout** the page picks from its content (src/lib/page/shape.ts):
-- Coat drive, a short story and nothing else, draws as the card at /coat-drive; Winter pantry, a
-- longer story and two tiers, as the letter at /winter-pantry; Saturday market, four tiers, two
-- questions and three photos beside its cover, as the feature at /saturday-market. each is live on
-- a settings row of its own, and the photos are small drawn PNGs stored in `image` and
-- `image_bytes`. the organisation's mission and vision fill About us on the feature and on the
-- Donation page, which the dashboard makes on first need with its one fixed layout.
--
-- **re-running it is safe.** the row is a singleton pinned to `default` by `org_profile_id_check`,
-- and the conflict arm fills only a column that is still empty — an EIN or an address typed on the
-- console since the first run survives every later one. every campaign, photo and settings row is
-- written under a fixed id and skipped where that id is already held. `legal_name` is NOT NULL, so a row that
-- exists already has one and the arm leaves it alone.
--
-- run it from the repository root, after the migrations:
--
--   pnpm db:migrate && pnpm db:seed

insert into org_profile (id, legal_name, tax_id, notification_email, mission, vision, created_at, updated_at)
values (
	'default',
	'Example Foundation',
	'12-3456789',
	'ops@example.org',
	'We get good food to every family in the valley. No forms, no questions, no one turned away.',
	'A valley where no one wonders where their next meal is coming from.',
	-- milliseconds, which is what `timestamp_ms` means on these two columns in
	-- src/lib/server/db/schema.ts — a row written in seconds reads as january 1970 on every screen.
	unixepoch() * 1000,
	unixepoch() * 1000
)
on conflict(id) do update set
	tax_id = coalesce(org_profile.tax_id, excluded.tax_id),
	notification_email = coalesce(org_profile.notification_email, excluded.notification_email),
	mission = coalesce(org_profile.mission, excluded.mission),
	vision = coalesce(org_profile.vision, excluded.vision),
	updated_at = excluded.updated_at;

